The first assertion ensures that if the `LastIndexOf(x)` for the old array was -1, then upon calling `IndexOf(x)`, the return value should be non-negative. Otherwise, it means `IndexOf(x)` did not find the element.

The second assertion checks the condition: "if an old array did not contain 'x', then the new array must contain 'x'." This is because when you use `IndexOf(x)` on the new array, it could either return the new index of "x" or return -1 (not found). The -1 case is ensured by the first assertion. 

